subquestions.solution:
In the S_z basis, the normalized S_{z'} eigenvector with m' = +1/2 is
$$
\begin{pmatrix}
\cos \frac{\theta}{2} \\
\sin \frac{\theta}{2}
\end{pmatrix}
$$
and the eigenvector with m' = -1/2 is
$$
\begin{pmatrix}
- \sin \frac{\theta}{2} \\
\cos \frac{\theta}{2}
\end{pmatrix}
$$
The initial state at t = 0+ is
$$
\begin{pmatrix}
1 \\
0
\end{pmatrix}
$$
The probability amplitudes are
$$
C_+ = \cos \frac{\theta}{2}
$$
$$
C_- = - \sin \frac{\theta}{2}
$$

For the stationary state, the Hamiltonian is $$H = -  rac{\hbar^2}{2 m} 
abla^2 + V$$ Use the variable change $$x =  rac{b}{R} \xi$$ $$y =  rac{b}{R} \eta$$ $$z =  rac{a}{R} \zeta$$ The boundary becomes $$\xi^2 + \eta^2 + \zeta^2 = R^2$$ The Laplacian transforms as $$
abla^2 =  rac{R^2}{b^2}  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \xi^2} +  rac{R^2}{b^2}  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \eta^2} +  rac{R^2}{a^2}  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \zeta^2}$$ To first order in  eta, using a \cong R  ig( 1 +  rac{2  eta}{3}  ig) and b \cong R  ig( 1 -  rac{ eta}{3}  ig), we have $$ rac{R^2}{b^2} \approx 1 +  rac{2  eta}{3}$$ $$ rac{R^2}{a^2} \approx 1 -  rac{4  eta}{3}$$ Hence the Hamiltonian becomes $$H \approx -  rac{\hbar^2}{2 m}  igg(  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \xi^2} +  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \eta^2} +  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \zeta^2}  igg) -  rac{\hbar^2  eta}{3 m}  igg(  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \xi^2} +  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \eta^2} - 2  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \zeta^2}  igg)$$ Identify $$H_0 = -  rac{\hbar^2}{2 m} 
abla^2$$ and $$H' = -  rac{\hbar^2  eta}{3 m}  igg(  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \xi^2} +  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \eta^2} - 2  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \zeta^2}  igg)$$ The first-order shift is $$\Delta E_0 = \langle \phi_0 | H' | \phi_0 angle$$ The ground state for the spherical well of radius R is $$\phi_0(r) = \sqrt{ rac{2}{R}}  rac{\sin  rac{\pi r}{R}}{r}$$ with $$r^2 = \xi^2 + \eta^2 + \zeta^2$$ By spherical symmetry, $$\langle \phi_0 |  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \xi^2} | \phi_0 angle = \langle \phi_0 |  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \eta^2} | \phi_0 angle$$ and $$\langle \phi_0 |  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \eta^2} | \phi_0 angle = \langle \phi_0 |  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \zeta^2} | \phi_0 angle$$ Define $$A = \langle \phi_0 |  rac{\partial^2}{\partial \xi^2} | \phi_0 angle$$ Then $$\langle \phi_0 | H' | \phi_0 angle = -  rac{\hbar^2  eta}{3 m} (A + A - 2 A)$$ Therefore $$\Delta E_0 = 0$$

